### Executive Summary

A hotfix plan for GH #483 (`qor/scripts/session.py` collapses a stale-but-valid
session marker with an absent one, silently rotating/reporting-missing a
session whose gate directory still holds unsealed, in-flight phase artifacts).
The full pre-audit lint ladder ran clean (7 of 7 grep-evidence citations
truth-checked after fixing one stale line-number citation and three malformed
citation pairings). `audit_risk_score` required Option B independent review
(author-momentum risk on a multi-entrypoint file); an architect-reviewer
subagent with only the plan content (no plan-authoring context) independently
re-verified every citation, the test-functionality of all seven planned unit
tests, the cyclic-import claim, the Feature Inventory Touches precedent, and
found no security/OWASP/Razor/dependency/macro-architecture/orphan violation. The
overall disposition is PASS at risk grade L1 (see the `## VERDICT` line above).
Full narrative: `docs/META_LEDGER.md` Entry #796.

